        {
          "type": "risk",
          "priority": "medium",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T12:48:07Z",
          "note": "MEDIUM — A04 (Insecure Design) / Trust Boundary: src/git/git-credentials.ts L104–111 (resolveCredential). The function's own JSDoc documents a known host/credential coherence gap: when credentialId is explicitly supplied, resolution performs an exact ID match with no cross-validation against the URL's hostname. This means a caller could (inadvertently or with elevated access) associate credential A (configured for host-a.example.com) with a repository whose URL resolves to host-b.example.com, and the token for host-a would be injected into requests to host-b. The API layer (PUT /credential) correctly validates that the referenced credentialId exists in appConfig.gitCredentials, but does NOT verify that credential.host matches the repository's URL host before allowing the association. Impact is limited to the local tool context (no remote attacker path under normal localhost binding), but the mismatch could cause an access token to be sent to an unintended host during git operations. Recommendation: In the PUT /api/repositories/:id/credential handler (repositories.ts L270–281), after confirming the credential exists, additionally assert that credential.host === extractHost(repo.Url) and return 400 if there is a mismatch, or at minimum surface a warning. The resolveCredential call sites in the orchestrators should also assert host coherence before injecting tokens."
