        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T12:48:07Z",
          "note": "INFO — A01 (Broken Access Control): The server binds exclusively to 127.0.0.1 (src/server/index.ts L180: server.listen(port, '127.0.0.1', ...)), which is the correct posture for a local developer tool. No network-exposed attack surface exists for the credential routes under normal operation. This is noted as a positive control."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T12:48:07Z",
          "note": "INFO — A02 (Cryptographic Failures / Token Masking): GET /api/repositories/:id/credential-options masks tokens with a flat '***' replacement (repositories.ts L332–334). The config endpoint (config.ts L28–30) uses a more informative 'maskToken' that reveals the last 4 characters. The difference in masking strategies between the two endpoints is an inconsistency but not a vulnerability — in the credential-options context, exposing the last 4 chars is unnecessary since the endpoint is only used to select which credential to associate. No action required."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T12:48:07Z",
          "note": "INFO — A03 (Injection): Token injection into git URLs is performed exclusively via WHATWG URL property assignment (parsed.username = token), never via string concatenation (git-credentials.ts L150–158). This correctly prevents URL injection for all token values, including those containing '@', '/', '#', or other special characters. Positive control confirmed."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T12:48:07Z",
          "note": "INFO — A01 (Path Traversal / Static Server): serveStatic() decodes percent-encoding before resolving the path and guards that the resolved absolute path starts with baseDir + sep (staticServer.ts L53–75). This correctly prevents %2e%2e path traversal. The X-Content-Type-Options and X-Frame-Options headers are set on all static responses, and a strict CSP (default-src 'self') is applied to HTML responses. Positive controls confirmed."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
